! Silicon at the settings of Elk's examples/TDDFT-time-evolution/Si-dielectric,
! for the real-time dielectric function (Calculator.get_realtime with a Kick of
! 0.1/c along x, which is that example's pulse, or get_realtime_dielectric).
!
! Matched to the Elk input: the lattice (avec 5.13 5.13 0, ..., so a = 10.26
! bohr), the LDA, the unshifted 8x8x8 grid. Not matched: the basis
! (norm-conserving plane waves at 16 Ry against LAPW at rgkmax = 7, with Elk's
! time evolution in a basis of 25 ground-state bands), and Elk's potential, which
! is updated at every step where this one is frozen. The scissor of the Elk
! example (0.0331 Ha) is refused by the real-time route here, so the
! like-for-like Elk run sets scissor 0 (si-dielectric-sc0.elk.in).
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.26, nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 16.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si 28.086 Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 8 8 8 0 0 0
